  "content": {
    "title": "Official: Barcelona starting lineup against Newcastle United | Champions League",
    "text": "Story byOfficial: Barcelona starting lineup against Newcastle United | Champions LeagueIn a little over an hour, FC Barcelona will square off against Newcastle United in the first leg of the UEFA Champions League Round of 16 at St James’ Park.With kick-off not far away, Barça head coach Hansi Flick has announced the starting lineup that will take the field, with plenty of changes to the team that faced Athletic Club over the weekend.AdvertisementKey midfielder Pedri is back in the team, replacing Marc Casado as the midfield partner of Marc Bernal, who has recovered from a stomach bug.Meanwhile, Ronald Araujo walks into the team at the expense of Eric Garcia, who misses out through muscular discomfort.The Uruguayan international is expected to partner with Pau Cubarsi at centre-back, while Joao Cancelo and Gerard Martin operate as the full-backs. Joan Garcia continues in goal.At the other end of the pitch, Robert Lewandowski gets the nod as the No. 9 for Barcelona, replacing Ferran Torres.Raphinha, who was also benched at the weekend, comes in for Marcus Rashford, while Lamine Yamal continues on the right. Fermin Lopez slots in as the No. 10 ahead of Dani Olmo.Story byBARCELONA, SPAIN - MARCH 18: Raphinha of FC Barcelona celebrates scoring his team's first goal during the UEFA Champions League 2025/26 Round of 16 Second Leg match between FC Barcelona and Newcastle United FC at Camp Nou on March 18, 2026 in Barcelona, Spain. (Photo by Judit Cartiel - UEFA/UEFA via Getty Images) | UEFA via Getty ImagesBarcelona and Arsenal could be set to meet in the Champions League this season if both teams make it through their quarter-final ties.The Catalan giants are up against Atletico in the next round, while Arsenal face a tricky test against Sporting Lisbon.AdvertisementArsenal topped the group phase with a 100% record but haven’t been at their best so far in 2026 and have just lost the Carabao Cup final to Manchester City.Former forward Paul Merson has spoken about the potential Champions League match-up and doesn’t fancy Arsenal’s chances following the loss to City.“It’s a sore one for Arsenal. It’s a confidence-sapping defeat because you come in the dressing room after that and think: oh my God, we just got destroyed in the second half,” he told Sky Sports.“Will it impact the Premier League? Arsenal are too good for the other teams they have to play against in the run-in, so they will beat those teams. But watching that game and that second half, I don’t see Arsenal winning anything else but the Premier League.Advertisement“Man City are still in the FA Cup. Watching that game, you’d be shocked if Arsenal went back to Wembley and beat them.“And then in the Champions League, I look at Barcelona – who Arsenal are on course to play in the semi-finals – and Arsenal haven’t got the pace to trouble Barcelona’s high line.“The forward players aren’t electric – they’re not like Anthony Elanga or Anthony Gordon who caused Barcelona problems in the last 16. I dread to think what Barcelona could do to Arsenal.”How do you think Barcelona would get on against Arsenal if they were to meet in the Champions League? Share your predictions in the comments below!",
